        "knowledge_point": "Calculating the Determinant of a NxN Matrix Using Cofactor Expansion",
        "problem": "Calculate the determinant of the matrix\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 6 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].$",
        "worked_solution": "We use the cofactor expansion along the first row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & ={a}_{11}{C}_{11}+{a}_{12}{C}_{12}+{a}_{13}{C}_{13}+{a}_{14}{C}_{14} \\\\  & =(-3)\\cdot {C}_{11}+0\\cdot {C}_{12}+0\\cdot {C}_{13}+5\\cdot {C}_{14} \\\\  & =-3{C}_{11}+5{C}_{14} \\\\  & =(-3)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-3 & ∗ & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & 0 & 3 & -2 \\\\ ∗ & -1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ ∗ & 6 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|+5\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}∗ & ∗ & ∗ & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & ∗ \\\\ 4 & -1 & 2 & ∗ \\\\ -1 & 6 & 0 & ∗\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-3)(-1)^{1+1}|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 6 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|+5(-1)^{1+4}|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 6 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 6 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|-5|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 6 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3(0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|-3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}|) \\\\  & -5(0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}|-0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}|+3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 6\\end{aligned}|) \\\\  & =-3\\cdot (-3\\cdot (0+18)+(-2)\\cdot (0-12))-5\\cdot (3\\cdot (24-1)) \\\\  & =90-345 \\\\  & =-255\\end{aligned}\n$$",
