    {
      "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14094816",
      "id": "q-129108",
      "status": "supported",
      "reason": null,
      "question": {
        "math_academy_id": "q-129108",
        "knowledge_point_id": "4f8fd8a4-1ca2-521d-8542-d11311bcc586",
        "knowledge_point": "Computing Variance Using the Definition Given a Probability Mass Function",
        "problem": "Let $X$ be the number obtained by a fair spinner with six sections labeled $-3,-1,2,3,5,12.$ What is $\\text{Var}[X]?$",
        "worked_solution": "The variance of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}(x-\\text{E}[X])^{2}\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute the probability mass function $f(x).$ Here, there are $6$ possible outcomes ($-3,-1,2,3,5,12$) and each outcome has the same probability, so the probability mass function is as follows:\n\n| $x$ | $-3$ | $-1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $5$ | $12$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ |\n\nNow, we need to compute $\\text{E}[X].$ Summing up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =(-3)\\cdot f(-3)+(-1)\\cdot f(-1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3)+5\\cdot f(5)+12\\cdot f(12) \\\\  & =(-3)(\\frac{1}{6})+(-1)(\\frac{1}{6})+2(\\frac{1}{6})+3(\\frac{1}{6})+5(\\frac{1}{6})+12(\\frac{1}{6}) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\text{E}[X]=3$ into the variance formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}(x-3)^{2}\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the variance as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =(-3-3)^{2}\\cdot f(-3)+(-1-3)^{2}\\cdot f(-1)+(2-3)^{2}\\cdot f(2)+(3-3)^{2}\\cdot f(3) \\\\  & +(5-3)^{2}\\cdot f(5)+(12-3)^{2}\\cdot f(12) \\\\  & =36\\cdot f(-3)+16\\cdot f(-1)+1\\cdot f(2)+0\\cdot f(3)+4\\cdot f(5)+81\\cdot f(12) \\\\  & =36(\\frac{1}{6})+16(\\frac{1}{6})+1(\\frac{1}{6})+0+4(\\frac{1}{6})+81(\\frac{1}{6}) \\\\  & =23\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        "answer_fields": [
