        "math_academy_id": "q-84023",
        "knowledge_point_id": "4f8fd8a4-1ca2-521d-8542-d11311bcc586",
        "knowledge_point": "Computing Variance Using the Definition Given a Probability Mass Function",
        "problem": "Let $X$ be the number obtained by a spinner with four sections labeled $1,2,3,4.$ The probability mass function $f(x)$ of $X$ is shown in the table below. What is $\\text{Var}[X]?$\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |",
        "worked_solution": "The variance of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}(x-\\text{E}[X])^{2}\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $\\text{E}[X].$ Summing up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3)+4\\cdot f(4) \\\\  & =1(\\frac{1}{3})+2(\\frac{1}{4})+3(\\frac{1}{6})+4(\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{7}{3}$ into the variance formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}{(x-\\frac{7}{3})}^{2}\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the variance as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & ={(1-\\frac{7}{3})}^{2}\\cdot f(1)+{(2-\\frac{7}{3})}^{2}\\cdot f(2)+{(3-\\frac{7}{3})}^{2}\\cdot f(3)+{(4-\\frac{7}{3})}^{2}\\cdot f(4) \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{9}\\cdot f(1)+\\frac{1}{9}\\cdot f(2)+\\frac{4}{9}\\cdot f(3)+\\frac{25}{9}\\cdot f(4) \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{9}(\\frac{1}{3})+\\frac{1}{9}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{4})+\\frac{4}{9}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{6})+\\frac{25}{9}(\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{18}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        "answer_fields": [
          {
