      "question": {
        "math_academy_id": "q-84200",
        "knowledge_point_id": "0e6a0c79-9597-5fca-9d41-305c541a7bdf",
        "knowledge_point": "Computing Variance Given a Probability Mass Function",
        "problem": "Let $X$ be the number obtained by a spinner with six sections labeled $1,2,3,4,5,6.$ The probability mass function $f(x)$ of $X$ is shown in the table below. What is $\\text{Var}[X]?$\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{3}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{16}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{16}$ |",
        "worked_solution": "We can compute the variance of a discrete random variable $X$ using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $\\text{E}[X].$ Summing up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3)+4\\cdot f(4)+5\\cdot f(5)+6\\cdot f(6) \\\\  & =1(\\frac{1}{8})+2(\\frac{1}{4})+3(\\frac{3}{8})+4(\\frac{1}{16})+5(\\frac{1}{8})+6(\\frac{1}{16}) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}].$ Summing up the products of each value of ${X}^{2}$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={1}^{2}\\cdot f(1)+{2}^{2}\\cdot f(2)+{3}^{2}\\cdot f(3)+{4}^{2}\\cdot f(4)+{5}^{2}\\cdot f(5)+{6}^{2}\\cdot f(6) \\\\  & =1(\\frac{1}{8})+4(\\frac{1}{4})+9(\\frac{3}{8})+16(\\frac{1}{16})+25(\\frac{1}{8})+36(\\frac{1}{16}) \\\\  & =\\frac{87}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{87}{8}-{3}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{87}{8}-9 \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
